== Usage ==
=== Time ===
A '''Huntrap''' can be placed in any location with available [[Attribute Shard]]s. The time to catch is random and based on the rarity of the shard caught.<ref name="trap-time"/>

{| class="wikitable" style="text-align:center;"
! Rarity !! Time
|-
|{{Common}} || 8-12 Hours
|-
|{{Uncommon}} || 10-15 Hours
|-
|{{Rare}} || 12-18 Hours
|-
|{{Epic}} || 14-21 Hours
|-
|{{Legendary}} || 16-24 Hours
|}

There are some ways to reduce the time to catch.

{| class="wikitable" style="text-align:center;"
!Source
!Modifier
|-
|[[#Huntraps|Huntrap]] || up to {{Green|-50%}}
|-
|[[Desert Temple]] || {{Green|-25%}}
|-
|{{Attr|Forest Trap}} || up to {{Green|-10%}} on Forest Shards
|-
|{{Attr|Combat Trap}} || up to {{Green|-10%}} on Combat Shards
|}

The bonus from the Huntrap Tier is calculated first then multiplied with all other modifiers which stack additively.<ref name="trap-speed"/><ref name="trap-speed-2"/>

This makes the minimum time multiplier {{Title|{{Green|0.325x}}|(0.5) * (1 -.25 -.1)}} for Forest and Combat Shards and {{Title|{{Green|0.375x}}|(0.5) * (1 -.25)}} for Water Shards.

